<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- W3C SCXML 3.13 and Appendix D's main event loop: a machine that reaches a
     top-level final state has exited the interpreter, and events that arrive
     afterwards are not processed. Refusing them is the clause. Being unable to
     say it happened is what this fixture is about.

     A host that sent an event and saw nothing move has three explanations, and
     until now it could tell apart only one of them:

       the event was dequeued and no transition matched
         -> `discarded_event_is_observable`'s axis; a count already answers

       the event was dequeued, a transition matched it, and that transition's
       guard evaluated false
         -> nothing moves and nothing is counted, correctly: a guard that says
            no is the document working

       the event was never dequeued at all, because the machine had stopped
         -> THIS axis, and before it, silence

     Measured 2026-08-22, and this is why the third one earns a fixture rather
     than a footnote. A consumer reported a guarded transition that "never
     fires" and spent four rewrites of the guard on it — every shape, ending
     with a trivially true arithmetic one. Driving the same document here fired
     it on the first attempt, at that consumer's own pinned revision. The guard
     was never the difference, and no accessor in any of the seven engines
     could have said what was.

     The document is deliberately thin, because the axis is about the ENGINE's
     door rather than about anything a document does. `poke` is handled by a
     targetless transition, so the datamodel counter is the only witness that a
     delivery ran anything at all — without it a passing run cannot be told
     apart from a run in which nothing fired. `finish` is what stops the
     machine. Everything after that is the axis.

     Deliberately single-axis: no delayed `<send>`, no `<invoke>`, no
     `<parallel>`, and no guard anywhere. A guard here would reintroduce the
     second explanation into a fixture whose whole point is separating it from
     the third.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" initial="working"
       name="unseen_event_is_reported">
    <datamodel>
        <data id="pokes" expr="0"/>
    </datamodel>
    <state id="working">
        <transition event="poke">
            <assign location="pokes" expr="pokes + 1"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="finish" target="done"/>
    </state>
    <final id="done"/>
</scxml>
